  "body": "## Result and scope\n\nIndependent finite semantic binding for **empty entrance E=0 and all 511\nhyperplane terminals U in F2^9**: the actual canonical-frame circuit and\nserialized child wrappers satisfy `L^-1 T_U R^-1 = C_[8] tensor I_2`, exactly\nincluding global phase and the wrapped coordinate chart's one spectator.\n\nThe retained HPE proof note records a local all-511 cold check but says its\nchecking script was not shipped. This package makes that source-side premise\nreproducible; the original finding retains credit. **No new Lean theorem,\nkernel execution, emitted-word replay, supplier adoption, invoice or kappa.**\n\n## Assignment, source binding and overlap\n\n- Track/card: independent-verification / `formal-interface-lemma`, refined to\n  the independent theorem-to-certificate binding method.\n- OS nonce `3b261ab51d51856a178fbaca68514f8a`; catalogue scope key\n  `e3ffea67887eeb4c396c`.\n- Base `d78fe4bbb6f6b769e39586f8bb3ba8c31a31fd3a`.\n- Exact object: generic `exact_cold` / `cold_hyperplane_width` in\n  `HyperplaneEnd/Multi.lean`, zero entrance, normals 1..511, source\n  `canonical_frame(9,U)` and serialized `lower_child` monomials.\n- Base-commit Git blobs and SHA256 pins are in SOURCES.json. Formal source\n  last-change commit `1db1fbe68cb5186899cf1fd691bc92056a845e49`; compiler\n  last-change commit `e07a8a3f9f79c22113398a0c5dbbc7601f489b3e`.\n- Entry survey and immediate concrete-term overlap refresh preceded\n  computation. Final refresh at 2026-10-14T07:13Z covered 385 open PRs and\n  337 discussions with complete pagination, plus local notes/ledger.\n- https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1415 is the three\n  non-cold C7/two-spectator pairs. Existing cold14 packages check fourteen\n  rank-four endpoints. Neither supplies this all-511 rank-eight audit.\n  No competing concrete binding was found; no novelty certificate claimed.\n- Claim: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1166#discussioncomment-18917564.\n\n## Evidence and independent method\n\nEvery annihilator kernel has 256 elements and an independently constructed\neight-vector basis. Every producer child reports rank eight and the zero\nentrance has an empty circuit. Candidate constructors internally use their\ntableau/zero-state machinery; neither is the independent acceptance oracle.\n\nA separately written Gaussian-integer literal evaluator and serialized inverse\nmonomial evaluator compare the wrapped operation against the closed-form C8\nkernel `16*(-i)^popcount(delta)` at common denominator256, with cross-spectator\nzeros. The encoded input uses radix2^18. A proved numerator coefficient bound\n4^8 plus reference bound16 gives difference digits <=65552 < radix-1, so exact\npacked equality forces all matrix entries to agree. This logically covers\n261632 complex-linear columns / 133955584 entries without storing those matrices.\nIt is not a claim that equality on an arbitrary single input proves equality.\n\nFive circuit faults reject, plus the unsafe-radix alias control. Optimized CLI\ntests reject omitted-hyperplane/unsafe-radix receipts and int/float or int/Boolean\nreceipt aliases with explicit diagnostics. The type-alias edge case was found\nin separate AI review, reproduced by failing tests and fixed by type-preserving\ncanonical JSON comparison. Fresh registered replay passed afterward.\n\nThe separate read-only AI mathematical/code reviews found no critical or\nimportant issue. The code reviewer independently expanded ordinary basis\ncolumns 0,1,255,256,511 at normals 1,257,511 using Gaussian/Fraction arithmetic:\n30 physical/wrapped equations and 15360 row entries agreed, including global\nphase and spectator identity. That review is not human or kernel review.\n\n## Files and reproduction\n\nAdds only `research/cold-hyperplane-semantic-binding/`:\n`README.md`, `TASK.json`, `SOURCES.json`, `VERIFY.json`, `RESULT.json`,\n`verify.py`, `test_verify.py`. Predecessor sources and selected record untouched.\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/cold-hyperplane-semantic-binding --check-only\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/cold-hyperplane-semantic-binding\n```\n\nObserved on Windows/Python3.12: metadata/pins PASS; two unittest groups PASS\n(79.309s); full registered replay PASS.\n\n```text\nPASS_COLD_HYPERPLANE_SEMANTIC_BINDING hyperplanes=511 columns=261632 entries=133955584 controls=5 global_phase spectator_preserved no_new_kappa\nPASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/cold-hyperplane-semantic-binding outcome=completed\n```\n\n## Remaining obligations and credit\n\nThis supplies external finite evidence for hE/hU in the stated operator model,\nnot a numeric-mask-to-Lean adapter or a proof term. Actual helper unit rows/\nzero columns, tails, recipes, chronology, footprints, whole-call hosting,\nprecision/tape, all-size compiler and analytic obligations are not rechecked.\nNo new moment or a<D/E improvement is claimed: the conditional width-eight\noperator interface is checked, not a new fully priced physical supplier.\nThe bounded next question in README/TASK is a formal normal-1 cold instance\nfollowed by a generic canonical-frame semantic bridge. No full cold replay or\nhosted-CI success is claimed.\n\nCredit Jeremy Kothe / jeremykothe2\n(https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/593), DreamingOfClouds\n(https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/599 and Lemma A/G/compiler\nlineage), commdata2338's independent non-cold binding\n(https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1415), icekylinx's retained\ncompiler package and the original cold14 source checks. No predecessor files\nare copied or edited. Prepared by **Aaron Wang / navinor, with help from\nchatgpt**, including substantial research, implementation, writing and separate\nread-only AI reviews. Apache-2.0.\n\nWorkflow feedback: the formal-pair survey prevented repeating a saturated\nnon-cold audit. The smallest/mixed probes succeeded before the complete family.\nNo directly fitting open handoff was found; the chosen card's source-binding\nroute was retained. No dependencies were installed. At the donor's request,\nthe temporary custom-location worktree will be cleaned after publication.\n",
